e Prime Minister  did yesterday you're both I know you we  booked it first  but it's a great venue  um you're both promising competence  economic stability and optimism  um you both appear to be battling for  the center ground how can you explain to  voters what is the real difference  between the two of you oh just look at  the last 13 years how can you seriously  come along  after 13 years of low growth 13 years of  Public Services being you know pushed to  their knees 13 years of you know  quashing aspirations of many people  across the country  um you know nobody really disputes that  our country is in a real state but it's  in a real mess  are to come along 13 years along the  line and say well I mean the Prime  Minister yesterday  it was almost as if it sort of suddenly  arrived from the Moon I was looking  around saying everything's busted  nothing working there was a real  commentary thing is there's a bit in  this speech where it says you know NHS  not working education not working  economy not working yeah and you've been  in bar for 13 years  um so that is the fundamental decision  no good coming along and making five  Bland promises and saying well just give  us another chance I'm sorry about the  last 13 years that's just not going to  wash with the British public  um thank you Camilla David from the  email  thanks very much  um your speech didn't mention  immigration uh particularly the issue of  small boats uh which the PM made a cast  iron Pledge on yesterday  um was it absent from your speech  because you don't have a plan  um and if you do have a plan what is it  well David we do have a plan and we've  set it out before many many times  um and it's a five-point plan but the  two most important as far as I'm  concerned are firstly I don't want  anybody crossing the channel in that way  nobody should want that anybody making  that dangerous Journey  the way to deal with that in my view is  to tackle the criminal gangs Upstream  criminal gangs are running this they're  running people to the Border in North  France and we have to tackle them at  source now when I was director of public  prosecutions we ran joint  um you know across Nation teams to deal  with transport of drugs and guns across  borders we can do it in relation to the  trafficking of people and the movement  of people across borders we can we can  go after those gangs and get them at  source that's the first thing the second  thing David is this  um the appalling delay in processing  Asylum applications  is at the heart of this  four percent of those that cross the  channel in small boats in 2021 have had  their Asylum claims processed  four percent when I first saw that  figure I couldn't believe it and that is  the state of our government and its  ability to grip this has to be measured  against their failure to tackle that  source and their absolute failure with  Asylum applications thank you David and  then Chloe from the eye  thank you  um on the subject of Take Back Control  Lisa and Andy told the eye earlier this  week that labor is looking to align with  EU laws in more areas than just security  and Veterinary standards when are we  going to get the full details of this  proposed new relationship and does this  mean that you're prepared to give up UK  sovereignty in some areas in order to  achieve those close to economic ties  well Chloe um we've set out I set out in  a speech I gave at the Irish Embassy  last year the sort of five principles  that we would apply in terms of  improving our relationship with the EU I  don't think anybody now seriously argues  um that this so-called oven-ready deal  is actually working for anyone and so of  course we have to address that and I'll  set that out in more detail but the five  principles that that'll be based on have  already been set out thank you very much  everybody thank you all for coming this  morning I'm really sorry to those of you  that had to stand who probably wanted me  to give shorter answers just now happy  New Year thank you very much  [Applause]
 

